I Dashboard). The tutorial packaging format is a shared contract that\n  the gallery code and both tutorial-content streams build against, so it is\n  defined once in its own epic rather than duplicated per consumer. The six\n  curated tutorials are authored content, split by component/owner: the five\n  workbench-centric journeys are notebook tutorials (Notebooks / Workbenches),\n  the pipeline journey is a pipeline tutorial (Data Science Pipelines /\n  RHOAI Pipelines). User-facing documentation is a separate docs-authoring\n  work stream (Documentation).\n- HLR-2's \"first RAG app\" tutorial is assumed notebook-based (it is one of the\n  workbench journeys); see Health Warnings.\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E002[\"E002 Tutorial packaging format\"] --> E001[\"E001 Dashboard gallery + launch\"]\n    E002 --> E003[\"E003 Notebook tutorial suite\"]\n    E002 --> E004[\"E004 Pipeline tutorial\"]\n    E001 --> E005[\"E005 Gallery + contribution docs\"]\n    E002 --> E005\n    E003 --> E005\n    E004 --> E005\n```\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| E002 → E001 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The gallery's launch mechanics parse the tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest) — Dashboard code builds against this contract, so the format must exist first. |\n| E002 → E003 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | Notebook tutorials are packaged, versioned, and validated per the format; content authoring consumes the framework. |\n| E002 → E004 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | The pipeline tutorial is packaged and validated per the same format. |\n| E001 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes the gallery as built. |\n| E002 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation of the contribution process describes the packaging format as defined. |\n| E003 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Contribution-process documentation references the notebook tutorial suite. |\n| E004 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Contribution-process documentation references the pipeline tutorial. |\n\nNo edge between E001 (gallery) and E003/E004 (tutorials): the tutorials are\ntestable independently of the Dashboard (that is the stated purpose of the\npackaging format), and the gallery reads packaged tutorials as content at\nexecution time — any coupling is expressed as acceptance criteria on E001\n(gallery launches tutorials packaged per the format), not as a DAG edge.\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n| HLR-1 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Gallery UI and one-click launch into the user's project. |\n| HLR-2 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E003, RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | Split by component/owner, not priority: notebook journeys (workbench, data prep, training, deployment, RAG) in E003; the pipeline journey in E004. Both are P0 halves of the same HLR. |\n| HLR-3 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Priority inheritance: E002 directly enables the P0 gallery (HLR-1) and both P0 tutorial epics (HLR-2), so E002 is P0 despite HLR-3 being P1. HLR-3 is NOT deferrable — the format is the shared contract all P0 work builds against; shipping it later would force every consumer to be rewritten. |\n| HLR-4 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | docs-authoring epic; priority derived from strategy frontmatter (Major → P1) per the docs-authoring priority exception, not inheritance. |\n\nAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n  Dependencies table, no formal Acceptance Criteria (Given/When/Then), no\n  Non-Functional Requirements, and the Affected Components list carries no\n  change descriptions or owner teams. Owner teams above were derived from the\n  architecture-context files (Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard, Notebooks →\n  Workbenches, Data Science Pipelines → RHOAI Pipelines). The Documentation\n  owner (\"RHOAI Docs\") is assumed — no architecture-context file exists for\n  Documentation; confirm with the stakeholder.\n- **Tutorial medium allocation unspecified**: HLR-2 enumerates six journeys\n  but does not state which are notebook tutorials and which are pipeline\n  tutorials. Assumed: the five workbench-centric journeys (first workbench,\n  data prep, first training run, first deployment, first RAG app) are notebook\n  tutorials; \"first pipeline\" is a pipeline tutorial. If the RAG tutorial (or\n  any other) turns out pipeline-based, move it between the two tutorial epics\n  — both epics exist either way, so this is a scope adjustment, not a\n  structural change.\n- **Tutorial content repository unspecified**: the strategy does not say where\n  curated tutorials live. The decomposition assumes they are authored in an\n  existing platform repo. If a new dedicated repository is required, a\n  repo-onboarding epic must be added ahead of the tutorial-content epics\n  (Rule 20 onboarding chain) — flag for the implementing teams.\n- **E003 size above the ~2-week guideline, recorded deliberately**: five\n  notebook tutorials is estimated at 2–4 weeks of authoring plus validation\n  runs. Kept as one epic because all five share the packaging format, the\n  validation harness, and a single content review cycle — splitting by\n  tutorial would duplicate harness wiring and fragment one review process.\n  Re-split trigger: re-split by journey group (e.g., workbench/deployment vs.\n  data-prep/training/RAG) if authoring exceeds ~4 weeks, if the tutorials\n  land in different repositories, or if validation turnaround forces\n  serialized rework across all five.\n- No priority inversions detected beyond the documented HLR-3 inheritance;\n  no scope traps beyond the repository note above.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing (the strategy\ndeclares no dependencies and no open questions).\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reas