ect with a single action, resulting in a workbench running the\n  tutorial's notebook with the pinned image specified by the tutorial\n  packaging.\n- From the gallery, a user can launch a pipeline tutorial into their own\n  project with a single action, resulting in the pipeline imported into the\n  project.\n- The gallery correctly renders and launches only tutorials that pass their\n  packaged validation status; invalid or missing tutorials are surfaced\n  without breaking the gallery.\n- Gallery and launch flows work for a user scoped to a single project via\n  OpenShift RBAC (no cluster-level permissions required).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n| HLR | Priority | Coverage |\n|-----|----------|----------|\n| HLR-1 | P0 | Full — the tutorial gallery and one-click launch into the user's project (workbench with notebook, or pipeline import). |\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":33274,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-95d54e5ad15f72a9","agent_id":"a628031f45560bd24","session_id":"d85f781e-f0ad-48f1-91fe-8221a9e97778","uuid":"78bcbb54-5eb8-4263-8f50-305a32f23b4a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:22:10.615Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9019 into epics"}
