ny Dashboard release.\n- Running the validation mechanism against a packaged tutorial produces a\n  deterministic pass/fail result against a target platform release.\n- The Dashboard gallery's launch mechanics and both tutorial-content work\n  streams can consume the format as specified without format changes\n  mid-stream (format is stable once agreed).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n| HLR | Priority | Coverage |\n|-----|----------|----------|\n| HLR-3 | P1 | Full — the packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest) making tutorials versioned and testable independently of Dashboard releases. Epic priority is P0 by inheritance: this format directly enables the P0 gallery (HLR-1) and the P0 curated tutorials (HLR-2). |\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":34036,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-95d54e5ad15f72a9","agent_id":"a628031f45560bd24","session_id":"d85f781e-f0ad-48f1-91fe-8221a9e97778","uuid":"41b3e3c6-8dd6-4abd-9214-589bfdbca24c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:22:20.718Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9019 into epics"}
