ng rules for packaged tutorials, so a tutorial can be updated and\n51\t    re-validated without a Dashboard release.\n52\t- Agreement on the format with the teams that consume it (Dashboard launch\n53\t  mechanics, notebook tutorial authoring, pipeline tutorial authoring) as\n54\t  part of normal design review.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- The packaging format specification defines tutorial metadata, pinned image\n59\t  references, and the validation manifest, and is reviewed by all three\n60\t  consuming work streams.\n61\t- A tutorial packaged per the format carries a version and can be re-versioned\n62\t  without any Dashboard release.\n63\t- Running the validation mechanism against a packaged tutorial produces a\n64\t  deterministic pass/fail result against a target platform release.\n65\t- The Dashboard gallery's launch mechanics and both tutorial-content work\n66\t  streams can consume the format as specified without format changes\n67\t  mid-stream (format is stable once agreed).\n68\t\n69\t## HLR Traceability\n70\t\n71\t| HLR | Priority | Coverage |\n72\t|-----|----------|----------|\n73\t| HLR-3 | P1 | Full — the packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest) making tutorials versioned and testable independently of Dashboard releases. Epic priority is P0 by inheritance: this format directly enables the P0 gallery (HLR-1) and the P0 curated tutorials (HLR-2). |\n74\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b627712fb80f5f7d","agent_id":"ab7e17e987796352d","session_id":"d85f781e-f0ad-48f1-91fe-8221a9e97778","uuid":"4965d4ca-b2c1-4c63-8ece-262bbee0ba4d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:24:51.283Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-831b6c474a96c6f2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
