ging format as defined. |\n65\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Contribution-process documentation references the notebook tutorial suite. |\n66\t| E004 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Contribution-process documentation references the pipeline tutorial. |\n67\t\n68\tNo edge between E001 (gallery) and E003/E004 (tutorials): the tutorials are\n69\ttestable independently of the Dashboard (that is the stated purpose of the\n70\tpackaging format), and the gallery reads packaged tutorials as content at\n71\texecution time — any coupling is expressed as acceptance criteria on E001\n72\t(gallery launches tutorials packaged per the format), not as a DAG edge.\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n75\t\n76\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n77\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n78\t| HLR-1 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Gallery UI and one-click launch into the user's project. |\n79\t| HLR-2 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E003, RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | Split by component/owner, not priority: notebook journeys (workbench, data prep, training, deployment, RAG) in E003; the pipeline journey in E004. Both are P0 halves of the same HLR. |\n80\t| HLR-3 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Priority inheritance: E002 directly enables the P0 gallery (HLR-1) and both P0 tutorial epics (HLR-2), so E002 is P0 despite HLR-3 being P1. HLR-3 is NOT deferrable — the format is the shared contract all P0 work builds against; shipping it later would force every consumer to be rewritten. |\n81\t| HLR-4 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | docs-authoring epic; priority derived from strategy frontmatter (Major → P1) per the docs-authoring priority exception, not inheritance. |\n82\t\n83\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n84\t\n85\t## Health Warnings\n86\t\n87\t- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n88\t  Dependencies table, no formal Acceptance Criteria (Given/When/Then), no\n89\t  Non-Functional Requirements, and the Affected Components list carries no\n90\t  change descriptions or owner teams. Owner teams above were derived from the\n91\t  architecture-context files (Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard, Notebooks →\n92\t  Workbenches, Data Science Pipelines → RHOAI Pipelines). The Documentation\n93\t  owner (\"RHOAI Docs\") is assumed — no architecture-context file exists for\n94\t  Documentation; confirm with the stakeholder.\n95\t- **Tutorial medium allocation unspecified**: HLR-2 enumerates six journeys\n96\t  but does not state which are notebook tutorials and which are pipeline\n97\t  tutorials. Assumed: the five workbench-centric journeys (first workbench,\n98\t  data prep, first training run, first deployment, first RAG app) are notebook\n99\t  tutorials; \"first pipeline\" is a pipeline tutorial. If the RAG tutorial (or\n100\t  any other) turns out pipeline-based, move it between the two tutorial epics\n101\t  — both epics exist either way, so this is a scope adjustment, not a\n102\t  structural change.\n103\t- **Tutorial content repository unspecified**: the strategy does not say where\n104\t  curated tutorials live. The decomposition assumes they are authored in an\n105\t  existing platform repo. If a new dedicated repository is required, a\n106\t  repo-onboarding epic must be added ahead of the tutorial-content epics\n107\t  (Rule 20 onboarding chain) — flag for the implementing teams.\n108\t- **E003 size above the ~2-week guideline, recorded deliberately**: five\n109\t  notebook tutorials is estimated at 2–4 weeks of authoring plus validation\n110\t  runs. Kept as one epic because all five share the packaging format, the\n111\t  validation harness, and a single content review cycle — splitting by\n112\t  tutorial would duplicate harness wiring and fragment one review process.\n113\t  Re-split trigger: re-split by journey group (e.g., workbench/deployment vs.\n114\t  data-prep/training/RAG) if authoring exceeds ~4 weeks, if the tutorials\n115\t  land in different repositories, or if validation turnaround forces\