{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c7c36a71ff9b33b","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\ttriage: null\n7\ttriage_rationale: null\n8\trevised: true\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary — RHAISTRAT-9019 (Curated getting-started tutorial gallery)\n11\t\n12\tTriage: neither Step 0 check fires. The strategy is not below-threshold — it\n13\tspans four components and, by its own problem statement, three architecturally\n14\tdistinct work streams (product code for the gallery and launch mechanics,\n15\tauthored tutorial content, and documentation) with different owners and review\n16\tprocesses. It is not docs-only — HLR-1/HLR-2/HLR-3 require product code and\n17\tauthored content. Full decomposition follows.\n18\t\n19\t## Epic List\n20\t\n21\t| ID | Title | Type | Component | Team | Priority | implementation_type |\n22\t|----|-------|------|-----------|------|----------|---------------------|\n23\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Tutorial gallery and one-click launch in the Dashboard | Implementation | Dashboard | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 | — |\n24\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Tutorial packaging format and validation manifest | Implementation | Dashboard | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 (inherited; HLR-3 is P1) | — |\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E003 | Curated notebook tutorial suite | Implementation | Notebooks | Workbenches | P0 | — |\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | Curated pipeline tutorial | Implementation | Data Science Pipelines | RHOAI Pipelines | P0 | — |\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | Tutorial gallery usage and contribution documentation | Implementation | Documentation | RHOAI Docs | P1 (docs-authoring priority exception: strategy priority Major → P1) | docs-authoring |\n28\t\n29\tRationale for boundaries:\n30\t\n31\t- The strategy states three kinds of work with different owners and review\n32\t  processes. The Dashboard gallery and launch mechanics are product code\n33\t  (RHOAI Dashboard). The tutorial packaging format is a shared contract that\n34\t  the gallery code and both tutorial-content streams build against, so it is\n35\t  defined once in its own epic rather than duplicated per consumer. The six\n36\t  curated tutorials are authored content, split by component/owner: the five\n37\t  workbench-centric journeys are notebook tutorials (Notebooks / Workbenches),\n38\t  the pipeline journey is a pipeline tutorial (Data Science Pipelines /\n39\t  RHOAI Pipelines). User-facing documentation is a separate docs-authoring\n40\t  work stream (Documentation).\n41\t- HLR-2's \"first RAG app\" tutorial is assumed notebook-based (it is one of the\n42\t  workbench journeys); see Health Warnings.\n43\t\n44\t## Dependency DAG\n45\t\n46\t```mermaid\n47\tgraph TD\n48\t    E002[\"E002 Tutorial packaging format\"] --> E001[\"E001 Dashboard gallery + launch\"]\n49\t    E002 --> E003[\"E003 Notebook tutorial suite\"]\n50\t    E002 --> E004[\"E004 Pipeline tutorial\"]\n51\t    E001 --> E005[\"E005 Gallery + contribution docs\"]\n52\t    E002 --> E005\n53\t    E003 --> E005\n54\t    E004 --> E005\n55\t```\n56\t\n57\t## DAG Justification\n58\t\n59\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n60\t|------|------|-----------|\n61\t| E002 → E001 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The gallery's launch mechanics parse the tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest) — Dashboard code builds against this contract, so the format must exist first. |\n62\t| E002 → E003 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | Notebook tutorials are packaged, versioned, and validated per the format; content authoring consumes the framework. |\n63\t| E002 → E004 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | The pipeline tutorial is packaged and validated per the same format. |\n64\t| E001 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation describes the gallery as built. |\n65\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Documentation of the contribution process describes the packaging format as defined. |\n66\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Contribution-process documentation references the notebook tutorial suite. |\n67\t| E004 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | Contribution-process documentation references the pipeline tutorial. |\n68\t\n69\tNo edge between E001 (gallery) and E003/E004 (tutorials): the tutorials are\n70\ttestable independently of the Dashboard (that is the stated purpose of the\n71\tpackaging format), and the gallery reads packaged tutorials as content at\n72\texecution time — any coupling is expressed as acceptance criteria on E001\n73\t(gallery launches tutorials packaged per the format), not as a DAG edge.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n76\t\n77\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n78\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n79\t| HLR-1 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E001 | Gallery UI and one-click launch into the user's project. |\n80\t| HLR-2 | P0 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E003, RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | Split by component/owner, not priority: notebook journeys (workbench, data prep, training, deployment, RAG) in E003; the pipeline journey in E004. Both are P0 halves of the same HLR. |\n81\t| HLR-3 | P1 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E002 | Priority inheritance: E002 directly enables the P0 gallery (HLR-1) and both P0 tutorial epics (HLR-2), so E002 is P0 despite HLR-3 being P1. HLR-3 is NOT deferrable — the format is the shared contract all P0 work builds against; shipping it later would force every consumer to be rewritten. |\n82\t| HLR-4 | P2 | RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | docs-authoring epic; priority derived from strategy frontmatter (Major → P1) per the docs-authoring priority exception, not inheritance. |\n83\t\n84\tAll four HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements.\n85\t\n86\t## Health Warnings\n87\t\n88\t- **Missing strategy sections**: the strategy has no Impacted Teams table, no\n89\t  Dependencies table, no formal Acceptance Criteria (Given/When/Then), no\n90\t  Non-Functional Requirements, and the Affected Components list carries no\n91\t  change descriptions or owner teams. Owner teams above were derived from the\n92\t  architecture-context files (Dashboard → RHOAI Dashboard, Notebooks →\n93\t  Workbenches, Data Science Pipelines → RHOAI Pipelines). The Documentation\n94\t  owner (\"RHOAI Docs\") is assumed — no architecture-context file exists for\n95\t  Documentation; confirm with the stakeholder.\n96\t- **Tutorial medium allocation unspecified**: HLR-2 enumerates six journeys\n97\t  but does not state which are notebook tutorials and which are pipeline\n98\t  tutorials. Assumed: the five workbench-centric journeys (first workbench,\n99\t  data prep, first training run, first deployment, first RAG app) are notebook\n100\t  tutorials; \"first pipeline\" is a pipeline tutorial. If the RAG tutorial (or\n101\t  any other) turns out pipeline-based, move it between the two tutorial epics\n102\t  — both epics exist either way, so this is a scope adjustment, not a\n103\t  structural change.\n104\t- **Tutorial content repository unspecified**: the strategy does not say where\n105\t  curated tutorials live. The decomposition assumes they are authored in an\n106\t  existing platform repo. If a new dedicated repository is required, a\n107\t  repo-onboarding epic must be added ahead of the tutorial-content epics\n108\t  (Rule 20 onboarding chain) — flag for the implementing teams.\n109\t- **E003 size above the ~2-week guideline, recorded deliberately**: five\n110\t  notebook tutorials is estimated at 2–4 weeks of authoring plus validation\n111\t  runs. Kept as one epic because all five share the packaging format, the\n112\t  validation harness, and a single content review cycle — splitting by\n113\t  tutorial would duplicate harness wiring and fragment one review process.\n114\t  Re-split trigger: re-split by journey group (e.g., workbench/deployment vs.\n115\t  data-prep/training/RAG) if authoring exceeds ~4 weeks, if the tutorials\n116\t  land in different repositories, or if validation turnaround forces\n117\t  serialized rework across all five.\n118\t- No priority inversions detected beyond the documented HLR-3 inheritance;\n119\t  no scope traps beyond the repository note above.\n120\t\n121\t## Tiered Delivery\n122\t\n123\tNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing (the strategy\n124\tdeclares no dependencies and no open questions).\n125\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d8892fd3800740b","agent_id":"aede6845dc81fa622","session_id":"d85f781e-f0ad-48f1-91fe-8221a9e97778","uuid":"ccba847c-c296-4e1e-b043-c3ea57125b31","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:29:05.823Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8c7c36a71ff9b33b","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-9019 decomposition"}
