{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-880e7212bacd54ba","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9019-E002\n3\ttitle: Tutorial packaging format and validation manifest\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 0\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Tutorial packaging format and validation manifest\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tThis epic defines the tutorial packaging format — the shared contract that\n34\tmakes curated tutorials versioned and testable independently of Dashboard\n35\treleases. The format specifies tutorial metadata, pinned images, and a\n36\tvalidation manifest. It is the framework the Dashboard gallery's launch\n37\tmechanics build against and that every curated tutorial is packaged,\n38\tversioned, and validated with. Defining it once here avoids three consumer\n39\twork streams each inventing their own packaging.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- A written specification of the tutorial packaging format covering:\n44\t  - tutorial metadata (identity, journey, display information, version);\n45\t  - pinned image references for tutorial execution;\n46\t  - a validation manifest describing how a tutorial is tested against a\n47\t    target platform release.\n48\t- A validation mechanism that executes the validation manifest for a packaged\n49\t  tutorial and produces a pass/fail result against a target release.\n50\t- Versioning rules for packaged tutorials, so a tutorial can be updated and\n51\t    re-validated without a Dashboard release.\n52\t- Agreement on the format with the teams that consume it (Dashboard launch\n53\t  mechanics, notebook tutorial authoring, pipeline tutorial authoring) as\n54\t  part of normal design review.\n55\t\n56\t## Acceptance Criteria\n57\t\n58\t- The packaging format specification defines tutorial metadata, pinned image\n59\t  references, and the validation manifest, and is reviewed by all three\n60\t  consuming work streams.\n61\t- A tutorial packaged per the format carries a version and can be re-versioned\n62\t  without any Dashboard release.\n63\t- Running the validation mechanism against a packaged tutorial produces a\n64\t  deterministic pass/fail result against a target platform release.\n65\t- Each consuming work stream — the Dashboard gallery's launch mechanics, the\n66\t  notebook tutorial authoring stream, and the pipeline tutorial authoring\n67\t  stream — confirms in writing at format sign-off that the format as\n68\t  specified meets its needs (one recorded sign-off per work stream); needs\n69\t  discovered after sign-off are met through the format's versioning rules\n70\t  rather than mid-stream format changes.\n71\t\n72\t## HLR Traceability\n73\t\n74\t| HLR | Priority | Coverage |\n75\t|-----|----------|----------|\n76\t| HLR-3 | P1 | Full — the packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation manifest) making tutorials versioned and testable independently of Dashboard releases. Epic priority is P0 by inheritance: this format directly enables the P0 gallery (HLR-1) and the P0 curated tutorials (HLR-2). |\n77\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d8892fd3800740b","agent_id":"aede6845dc81fa622","session_id":"d85f781e-f0ad-48f1-91fe-8221a9e97778","uuid":"02ee977b-49ac-47c9-98d0-54afbc7eff45","timestamp":"2026-10-26T15:29:08.913Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-880e7212bacd54ba","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","s